Generic single-database configuration with an async dbapi.

## Commands

Run these from the repo root (so `load_dotenv()` picks up `.env` for `DATABASE_URL`).

```
# Create a new migration from changes made to the models in src/server/db/base.py
.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m alembic revision --autogenerate -m "short description"

# Apply all migrations up to the latest
.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m alembic upgrade head

# Roll back the most recent migration
.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m alembic downgrade -1

# Show the migration currently applied to the database
.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m alembic current

# List all migrations and their order
.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m alembic history
```

Always review an autogenerated revision file before applying it — autogenerate reliably
catches new/dropped tables and columns, but misses things like renames (sees them as a
drop + add).